(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #114, the undefined-cast fallback: `<number> as a
 list` has no meaning, unlike the four scalar<->scalar casts above. A
 number value read into a `list` slot raises the error flag and takes the
 destination's own empty value - the same answer #91 already gives a
 missed read - rather than storing the number's raw bits as a list
 pointer and segfaulting on first use.)

